    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `locality` derivation from city using the fixed city-to-region table.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `locality` property to the `Owner` schema (the DTO is code-generated from this spec at build time), documenting the fixed mapping and the `UNKNOWN` fallback.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping(target = \"locality\", ...)` on `toOwnerDto` plus a `toLocality(owner)` derivation backed by the fixed `CITY_REGION` table (`Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD`), returning `\"UNKNOWN\"` for any other city. This mirrors the existing derived-field pattern used for `membershipTier`/`membershipNumber`.\n\nThe derivation flows through the existing `GET /api/owners/{ownerId}` pipeline (`LoadOwner` \u2192 `RespondWithOwner`) with no wiring changes needed.\n\n**Tests:** `AcceptanceTest` (the only test class) passes \u2014 both `coreDerivesRegionForKnownCity` (Sydney \u2192 `NSW`) and `functionalityUnknownCityIsUnknown` (random city \u2192 `UNKNOWN`) are green, and `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
